d center of Heliopolis, with beautiful Andalusian style architecture and lots of old churches and cultural centres from the days of cosmopolitan, multicultural Cairo."],["Baron Empain Palace","sight",30.08667,31.33028,"al-Uruba St","","","","","r","Erected by Baron Empain, this utterly bizarre structure was inspired by Angkor Wat and the Hindu temples of Odisha, and looks thoroughly out of place in Cairo. You can take a peek from the road, but alas, the interior has been off…"],["Basilica of Notre Dame","sight",30.09358,31.32512,"at the end of Al-Ahram Street","","","","","r","A miniature version of Istanbul's Ayasofya, dubbed the \"jelly mold\" by expats. Especially worth a look."],["Uruba Presidential Palace","sight",30.08833,31.32,"","Not open to the public","","","","r","Once a grand hotel that opened in 1910, the Uruba Palace is now the official residence of the Egyptian President. The hotel fell into disuse in the 1960s, and for a brief period, the palace was home to the Federation of Arab Republics.…"],["Korba Street Festival","activity",30.09068,31.32327,"Baghdad Street","","","","","r","Annual cultural festival that takes place each spring, centering on Heliopolis’ Baghdad Street. The festival features Egyptian performing artists."],["Petit Palmyra","restaurant",30.09228,31.32357,"27 al-Ahram Street","noon-1AM","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"]]}